|> 
|>     I've recently been wondering what determines the type of shop generated
|> in Nethack. I've never seen it mentioned before but there seems to be a clear
|> pattern. General stores seem to be the most common (perhaps %50?). Next seem

                                                                ^^ good guess

|> to come weapons and armor stores. Less common are bookstores, liquor stores
|> and delicatessans. Hardware stores, jewelry stores and apparel shops (wands)
|> seem to be the rarest. Anyone know the details on this from the source?
|> 
|> 
|>                               David Rodriguez
|> 

General Store:                  44%  (47% ifndef spells)
Used Armor Dealership:          14%
Second Hand Bookstore:          10%
Liquor Emporium:                10%
Antique Weapons Outlet:          5%
Delicatessen                     5%
Jewelers                         3%
Quality Apparel and Accessories: 3% (I've never seen one)
Hardware Store:                  3%
Rare Books                       3% (NA ifndef spells)


Also, if the shop is "big", it is not allowed to be a wand shop or a
book shop -- these are turned into general stores.

See mkroom.c, mkroom.h, and shknam.c for more details.

